s/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-05T17:18:04Z","updated_at":"2026-05-05T17:18:04Z","body":"Could you describe the migration path outside of godot-cpp? `is_class()` is just a class check, it doesn't provide casting functionality.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp/pull/1974 now uses `is_class()` + `static_cast`, but the latter doesn't exist in all languages (C, Go, Rust...). Since bindings can no longer obtain a pointer through `object_cast_to()`, will the original pointer always be valid? Or is the idea that downcasts are implemented purely on binding side?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4381478052/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4381695289","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119254#issuecomment-4381695289","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119254","id":4381695289,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBStdOQ","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-05T17:50:57Z","updated_at":"2026-05-05T17:50:57Z","body":"`object_cast_to()` never did any actual casting. All it did was check if a cast was possible, and if so, return the same pointer; if not, return `nullptr`. So, the recommendation here is just to do the check with `is_class()` instead. Any actual casting has always been handled on the binding side","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4381695289/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4381700028","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119254#issuecomment-4381700028","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119254","id":4381700028,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBStvvA","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-05T17:51:43Z","updated_at":"2026-05-05T17:51:43Z","body":"> Could you describe the migration path outside of godot-cpp? `is_class()` is just a class check, it doesn't provide casting functionality.\r\n> \r\n> [godotengine/godot-cpp#1974](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp/pull/1974) now uses `is_class()` + `static_cast`, but the latter doesn't exist in all languages (C, Go, Rust...). Since bindings can no longer obtain a pointer through `object_cast_to()`, will the original pointer always be valid? Or is the idea that downcasts are implemented purely on binding side?\r\n\r\nYes, downcasts are expected to be implemented purely on the binding side. You can expect the pointer to be stable (`T *` will always be equal to `Object *`).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4381700028/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4382448881","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119254#issuecomment-4382448881","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godo